{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-13T09:57:53.544Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_provenance":{"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-rust-oracle-recovery-167"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Track deferred close recovery evidence compatibility"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Follow-up to PR 165 review thread PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs63A9qa. The exact blank-evidence delimiter command withdraws suggested retries in both published 2026.11.11 and native output; its byte comparison is pinned. Separately, the emitted update advice uses --resolution, --expected-result and --actual-result: the published CLI accepts these flags but native update refuses them. Track that compatibility gap under issue 167 without changing the accepted refusal policy in this round. Evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/issues/167#issuecomment-6849115850. Add native execution coverage for the emitted advice when implementing the follow-up."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Task"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["gh:unbraind/pm-rust#167","oracle","recovery"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-13T09:57:53.544Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-13T09:57:53.544Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"codex-agent"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Execute emitted close recovery advice successfully against native and published trackers while preserving exact refusal envelopes."}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"d10dc4f417c1ad3aaa31a549b3e4130f728c0c9e2cb19353a289e0dc73bd0d4d","item_hash_version":3,"message":"explicit_unset=assignee","event_class":"substantive","record_hash_versi